epository root run `npm install` so package-lock.json picks up the new workspace (CI uses `npm ci`, which fails if the lock file is out of sync), then run `npm ci` and `npm test` and make sure both succeed. Commit package-lock.json with the change.\n9. Open exactly one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test with all of the above. The PR body must contain the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow to finish on the PR head commit and confirm it is green; if it fails, fix it on the same branch and push until it is green.","verifier":"Check out the PR head commit and run every command from the repository root after `npm ci`. Use a scratch directory from `mktemp -d` for fixture files. Run one check per expect line below, in order, and report PASS or FAIL for each with the evidence (commands and output).\n\n## Check 1\nExpect: packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\nRun:\n- Clean: `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n[2]\\n' > $T/clean.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/clean.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"`\n- Bad rows: `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{bad\\n   \\n\"ok\"\\n{\"torn\":' > $T/bad.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/bad.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"` (line 3 `{bad` is invalid, lines 2 and 4 are blank/whitespace, line 6 is an unterminated invalid last line).\n- Valid unterminated last line: `printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}' > $T/end.jsonl; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js $T/end.jsonl; echo \"exit=$?\"`\nPASS if: clean.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0; bad.jsonl prints exactly two error lines, one starting `$T/bad.jsonl:3: ` and one starting `$T/bad.jsonl:6: `, each followed by a non-empty error text, with no error line for lines 2 or 4, and exits 1; end.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 